1
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,360
YAMU!

2
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:28,177
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:29,520
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

5
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:02,757
I can't believe Yugi-Moto
agreed to give up

6
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,537
Duel Monsters forever if
he loses at this new game.

7
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:10,500
I know, especially since Dungeon Dice
Monsters is a game his opponent invented.

8
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:12,250
Duel's best!

9
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:14,101
Joey's lost now, he's Duke's pet!

10
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,480
The dumbest dog you've ever met!

11
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:18,010
And now!

12
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:20,200
Uh-oh, it's a rabbit dog!

13
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:22,636
Guess we'll have to get him a muzzle!

14
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,777
No, no, no, that won't
be necessary, girls.

15
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:28,677
Why don't y 'all just go back to cheering
for your little dookie over there?

16
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,525
Here, I'll even start you off.

17
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,480
Duke, Duke, he's so great.

18
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:33,720
Make no mistake.

19
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:35,470
Man,

20
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:37,757
I can't wait till Yugi
wins this and gets Joey out

21
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:40,777
of that stupid dog suit Duke
Devlin's making him wear.

22
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,380
That guy's a real jerk.

23
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:46,677
Yeah, Duke's all about humiliating
his opponents, especially Yugi.

24
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:50,297
Why else would he want to beat him
in a game broadcast around the world?

25
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,020
He's sure on a vendetta.

26
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:53,960
It's not fair.

27
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:55,577
He blames Yugi for everything.

28
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:57,380
Is game not taking off?

29
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:59,377
Losing Pegasus as his business partner?

30
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,237
It's just wrong. You! Come on, buddy,

31
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,197
you just gotta win this
match and get me out of

32
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:08,040
this fleabag costume before
I completely lose it! Hey!

33
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,340
Down, boy!

34
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,700
Bad dog!

35
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:16,800
I'm... not... a dog!

36
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,500
I wish I could just play dead.

37
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:26,031
Man, those cheerleaders sure
know how to yank Joey's chain.

38
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:29,848
Yeah, well, at least they haven't
reduced him to howling yet.

39
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,600
I'm not housebreaking him.

40
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,977
Duke's monsters have already taken
out one of my three heart points.

41
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,837
And unless I do something right
here, they'll take out another.

42
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,744
I have to make this turn count.

43
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:45,685
But I think I just found
what I needed to know.

44
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,257
Go, dice roll!

45
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,740
Come on.

46
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,097
I need to get some Magic Crests here.

47
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:54,592
Otherwise, I may not be able
to win Joey his freedom back.

48
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:57,090
There's one.

49
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,060
And another.

50
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,460
Two out of three. Great.

51
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,257
It appears I've rolled
two Magic Crests, Duke.

52
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:09,137
But since both have times two multiplier
emblems, each of their values are doubled,

53
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:10,877
giving me four Magic Crests,

54
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,217
more than enough to activate
Thunderball's special ability.

55
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,137
Not bad.

56
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:18,077
You've even learned how to
use your help screen to find

57
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:21,219
out how to activate the
monster's special abilities.

58
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:22,480
That's right.

59
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:28,481
Now I'll use three of the crests I rolled
and activate Thunderball's special attack.

60
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:32,240
Go, Rolling Crush!

61
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:35,800
Your blast lizard is
about to be bowled over.

62
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,677
But my attack will not end there.

63
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:43,697
I'll use three more Magic
Crests I saved in my

64
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:46,600
Crest Pool and have
Thunderball strike again!

65
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:48,610
Thunderball!

66
00:03:48,693 --> 00:03:49,523
Attack!

67
00:03:49,606 --> 00:03:50,436
Gator Dragon!

68
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,100
You nailed him!

69
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,104
Way to pick up the spare, Yook!

70
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:56,370
Yookie!

71
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:58,120
Great job!

72
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,640
Okay, Duke.

73
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,320
Now we have a game.

74
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,920
Hey, cool! Let me see! Come on!

75
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:13,440
That new store certainly
has a crowd today.

76
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,340
I wonder just what my
competition is up to.

77
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:18,980
Excuse me.

78
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,977
Age before beauty is coming through.

79
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,472
Hey, what are you doing?

80
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,200
Marvelous. Splendid.

81
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,500
Beautiful even.

82
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,860
I'm in love.

83
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,420
Oh, what I wouldn't give
for a TV of this size.

84
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:35,240
Is that Joey?

85
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,110
Taya?

86
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,670
Yuki?

87
00:04:38,753 --> 00:04:40,140
Oh, it's not enough.

88
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,908
They take my business,
but my grandson, too.

89
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:48,124
No one's here to watch
the back your head, dude.

90
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,808
Move it or lose it, Popsie.

91
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,440
Not bad, Yu-Gi.

92
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:57,397
You used that help screen to come up
with a pretty impressive move there.

93
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:01,068
But still, I wouldn't get any
ideas about winning this match.

94
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,937
You'll never know Dice
Monsters as well as I do.

95
00:05:04,020 --> 00:05:06,497
After all, I'm the guy
who invented the game.

96
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:07,520
That's true.

97
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:11,506
Just as your idol Pegasus invented
the Duel Monsters card game.

98
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:16,114
But inventing a game doesn't mean that
you can't be beaten at it, Devlin.

99
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:21,517
But perhaps my beating Pegasus
was the exception to the rule.

100
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,953
Perhaps you are better.

101
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,740
Why, thank you.

102
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,580
Hey, wait.

103
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:28,697
You only beat Pegasus by cheating.

104
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:31,100
Don't try and fool me. No, Duke.

105
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:32,752
You're fooling yourself.

106
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,280
Yeah, right, cheat.

107
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,220
Go! Dice roll!

108
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,390
Nice.

109
00:05:41,473 --> 00:05:43,321
I'll save those in my crest pool.

110
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:46,300
Now it's my turn, Duke. Go! Dice roll!

111
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,160
Way to go, Yugi! Excellent.

112
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:52,401
Two summons and a movement crest.

113
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:54,320
Dimension the dice!

114
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:58,620
Now, behold the monster
that I've unlocked.

115
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:03,240
I've summoned the Knight of Twin Swords!

116
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:06,005
For all the good it'll do you.

117
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:09,414
None of my monsters are within
striking distance of him.

118
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:13,329
That's why I'll store my other
die in my crest pool for now.

119
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:18,437
So, at least you've become
skilled at conserving your crest.

120
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:19,377
It's about time.

121
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:23,200
Man, crest this, crest that, I'm
totally lost. Guess it's true.

122
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:26,007
You really can't teach
an old dog new tricks.

123
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,820
Come on, dog boy.

124
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,657
It's Dungeon Dice rules number one.

125
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,857
You're allowed to take the crest you roll,

126
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:35,352
store them in your crest pool,
and then use them later on.

127
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:36,350
Aw, yeah!

128
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,757
I remember that rule now!

129
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:39,117
Concentrate on dog rules!

130
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:42,357
If you're gonna learn, learn
how to obey our commands.

131
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,360
Right now, sit, dog boy.

132
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,440
Boy, that's rough.

133
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,759
It's a dog's life.

134
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:55,140
There Yugi goes again,
scouring that help screen.

135
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:57,077
He's certainly a quick study.

136
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:57,990
I'll give him that.

137
00:06:58,073 --> 00:07:02,314
Some of the things he's learned in
minutes took me weeks to come up with.

138
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,617
I'll just have to take things up a notch,

139
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:07,288
and I have just the
dice to do it with, too.

140
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,800
My turn now!

141
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:10,420
Go dice roll!

142
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:12,920
All right!

143
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,728
A pair of summoning crests!

144
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,420
Dimension the dice!

145
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:18,500
And unlock my creature!

146
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:24,780
Now here's a monster your knight will
definitely want to steer clear of.

147
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:26,297
The Battle Ox!

148
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:30,777
But then you may have a hard time
avoiding him once I use these

149
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:34,700
four stored movement press and
have him charge in for an attack.

150
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:39,220
Here he comes, Yu-Gi, invading your turf.

151
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:42,560
And you better believe this
bull knows how to fight.

152
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:46,560
Now, Battle Ox, go for the
Knight of Twin Swords, attack!

153
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,220
Oh, and by the way,

154
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:52,357
my ox gains a ten-point bonus when
attacking all warrior-type creatures,

155
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:53,560
like your knight.

156
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,590
Knight!

157
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:57,940
Quickly, switch into defense mode.

158
00:07:58,420 --> 00:07:59,620
Just in time.

159
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:04,537
Sorry, Devlin, but in defense mode,
my knight has a defense power of 10.

160
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:08,326
Meaning that your ox's attack
will only do 20 points of damage.

161
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:12,920
He'll lose 20 of his 30 hit
points from your ox's attack,

162
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,480
but he'll still remain on the board.

163
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,090
Unbelievable.

164
00:08:18,173 --> 00:08:19,717
That cheat has taught
himself how to defend.

165
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,780
It's my turn.

166
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,120
Go, dice roll!

167
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:26,457
I'm activating my knight's special ability

168
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:30,357
By using both these attack crests Now he's

169
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,997
allowed to attack you
twice in one turn And

170
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,668
make two assaults on
your beast's hit points

171
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,360
Go double slash attack

172
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:44,100
Face it, Duke Your ox has been gored

173
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:52,580
No, my ox That knight
slaughtered him No, Dookie-Boo!

174
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:57,180
Way to go, Yugi.

175
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,399
You're really on a roll now, buddy.

176
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:01,210
Yugi!

177
00:09:01,293 --> 00:09:02,123
Great move!

178
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:07,171
Your turn, Duke, but this time you might
want to steer clear of my monsters.

179
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:17,960
So you were able to defeat
my battle-ox, Yugi. So what?

180
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,577
My last brilliant move wasn't about
just creating another monster.

181
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:25,131
It was about building out my dungeon path.

182
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,070
Your dungeon?

183
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:27,300
That's right.

184
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:30,562
Just take a look at your
dungeon path, you dunce.

185
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:31,956
What about it, Duke?

186
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,551
I'll tell you what, Yugi.

187
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,976
It's been stopped dead in its tracks.

188
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,520
See my red dungeon path?

189
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,477
Do you see how it reaches from one side of

190
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,217
the board all the way across to the other,

191
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:48,300
creating one solid line in
front of your blue path?

192
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,637
Well, guess what, Yu-Gi?

193
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,477
Your dungeon path can't cross it,

194
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:53,757
and that means that
your monsters can't get

195
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,617
to my heart points on
the other side of it.

196
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:57,000
You're stuck, Yu-Gi.

197
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:59,997
You can't build your dungeon
path forward anymore.

198
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,480
You're completely boxed in. No!

199
00:10:02,860 --> 00:10:03,801
He's trapped me!

200
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:14,106
Duke's laid out his dungeon path so it
completely blocked my ability to advance.

201
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:15,700
I am trapped.

202
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,620
What's going on here?

203
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:22,255
I'm not sure I follow it myself, Taya.

204
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:26,400
I'll explain one last time. It's simple.

205
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:30,877
My red dungeon path extends from one side
of the board all the way to the other.

206
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:33,797
Now, since one dungeon
path can't overlap another,

207
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,540
and Yugi's blue path is behind my red one,

208
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:39,777
Yugi can no longer continue
to build his path forward.

209
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:43,480
But if all of Yugi's monsters
are stuck behind that dungeon,

210
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:47,582
then they can't get to Duke's heart
points, and that would mean...

211
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,060
That I'm stuck in his costume.

212
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:52,717
And that the so-called
king of games over there

213
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,565
is about to be forced
into an early retirement.

214
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:58,317
There's got to be some
way Yugi can still win.

215
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,871
Well, actually, there is.

216
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:03,777
Yugi could always try cruising his
monsters through my dungeon path.

217
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:05,337
He can move through your path?

218
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:06,250
Sure,

219
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:08,937
if he doesn't mind running his
monsters through a virtual gauntlet,

220
00:11:09,020 --> 00:11:10,377
because to get to my heart points,

221
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:14,117
he'll have to survive every one of
my monsters that he meets on the way.

222
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,030
Every one?

223
00:11:15,113 --> 00:11:17,637
But then that means all his
monsters would get pulverized.

224
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,550
No joke.

225
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:20,060
My roll now.

226
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:22,900
Oh, perfect.

227
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:26,840
Just perfect.

228
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,100
Know what this is, Yugi?

229
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,960
Looks like a black dye.

230
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:33,737
A very rare black dye, to be exact.

231
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:37,440
And with it, I'm going to finish
you off and win this game.

232
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,400
Go! Dice roll!

233
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:45,540
Well, what is it?

234
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,840
A pair of summons.

235
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:50,520
Dimension the dice!

236
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:53,780
Now you'll see the power
of the rare black dice.

237
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:56,220
Oh, boy.

238
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:59,226
What's Yugi going to
have to contend with now?

239
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:02,950
Behold!

240
00:12:03,033 --> 00:12:04,420
The Warp Vortex!

241
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:07,600
Warp what?

242
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:09,380
Warp Vortex.

243
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:12,212
Guess I'll have to explain this now, too.

244
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:15,077
The dark hole you see
before you is a special

245
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:17,997
summoning that only a rare
black dye can produce.

246
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,520
It's a cosmic portal.

247
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:23,437
When monsters jump into it, they're sent
to another place on the board instantly.

248
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:27,297
This other place is determined by
wherever the second vortex is laid.

249
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:29,277
That's where the monster pops out.

250
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:33,360
It takes two vortexes to complete
the circuit, creating a warp tube.

251
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,497
And guess what, Yugi?

252
00:12:34,580 --> 00:12:37,037
I've already got the second
location all picked out.

253
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:40,057
Deep within your territory
and well behind your defenses.

254
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:44,500
It's the perfect spot for easy access
to your heart points. Now, Yugi,

255
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:47,657
all that stands between you
and defeat is the time that it

256
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:51,211
